# Example Ly-alpha mean-intensity profile for the TPM.py H-alpha module.
# Set  Jlya_file = path + '/Jlya.txt'  in TPM.py and copy this file there.
#
# Two whitespace-separated columns:
#   col 1 : r / R_p   -- radial coordinate, SAME as ATES output (r column
#                        of Ion_species/Hydro_ioniz; r/R_p, starts near 1)
#   col 2 : J_lya     -- Ly-alpha mean intensity J_nu at line center,
#                        in cgs: erg s^-1 cm^-2 Hz^-1 sr^-1
#
# J_lya drives the 1s->2p radiative pumping (Christie, Arras & Li 2013,
# ApJ 772, 144), which sets the n=2 hydrogen population and hence the
# H-alpha absorption. Values are interpolated onto the ATES grid and
# clamped to the endpoints outside this file's range.
#
# (The numbers below are an illustrative ~1/r decline; replace with your
#  own radiative-transfer / Christie-style estimate of J_lya(r).)
  1.00   3.00e-11
  1.50   2.00e-11
  2.00   1.50e-11
  3.00   1.00e-11
  5.00   6.00e-12
 10.00   3.00e-12
